  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR replaces #3949, as requested in its latest review. It preserves the original kernel test diff.\nThe new branch starts at upstream main `d94b9816d55043e3a578dea490f6f7d3be31d154`.\nIts only commit uses `Refs #2578`. It contains no closing keyword for that issue.\n\nThe test `blend::a_design_with_a_fillet_imports_its_blend_body` checks a generated blend body through import.\nIt checks the blend face, volume, bounds, mesh closure, and mesh volume deviation.\nThe decision note keeps the release fixture and STEP comparison open.\nIssue #2578 must stay open for those acceptance checks.\n\n## Validation\n\nFinal head: `8c3606da03a1c2e4334eb057c9e51b27d791667f`.\n\n- History pin: the check rejects a closing keyword for #2578 in any PR commit and requires `Refs #2578`.\n- Mutation proof: old head RED, replacement head GREEN, old head RED, replacement head GREEN.\n- The original and replacement source test diffs are byte-identical against their respective merge bases.\n- The earlier decoder refusal mutation made the blend test fail. Restoring the decoder made it pass, as recorded in #3949.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 1 step, all 8 kernel import tests passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: RED, 1 step; 41 passed, 2 failed, 4 ignored. Both failures were 60-second timeouts in `catalog_3d_rough_finish::{rebuilds,regenerates}`. Neither reported a golden mismatch.\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog -- --test-threads=1`: GREEN, 43 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored. The two timeout cases passed in 57.738s and 56.254s. This serial rerun checks contention; the original parallel gate result remains RED.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNo recorded programs changed. The catalog suite was run; the timeout results are listed above.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe current SolidCraft release fixture and STEP comparison remain open.\nHeavy lanes do not apply. This diff changes only kernel tests and a decision note.\nThe diff changes no motion, simulation, post, geometry, application operation, or UI code.\nUI screenshots do not apply.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #2578\n",
